Table full name: TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
Column name: Codons Type: TEXT Description: Alternative codons with the variant base in upper case
Column name: AA_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in NHLBI-ESP African American population
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: CANONICAL Type: TEXT Description: A flag (YES) indicating that the VEP-based canonical transcript, the longest translation, was used for this gene, if not, the value is null
Column name: dbSNP_RS Type: TEXT Description: Rs-IDs from the dbSNP database, novel if not found in any database used, or null if there is no dbSNP record, but it is found in other databases
Column name: PUBMED Type: TEXT Description: Pubmed ID(s) of publications that cite existing variant
Column name: project_short_name Type: TEXT Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; eg. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: CLIN_SIG Type: TEXT Description: Clinical significance of variant from dbSNP
Column name: SOMATIC Type: TEXT Description: Somatic status of each ID reported under Existing_variation (0, 1, or null)
Column name: SWISSPROT Type: TEXT Description: UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot accession
Column name: Existing_variation Type: TEXT Description: Known identifier of existing variation
Column name: Variant_Classification Type: TEXT Description: Translational effect of variant allele
Column name: AMR_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined American population
Column name: STRAND Type: NUMBER Description: DNA strand (1 or -1) on which the transcript/feature lies
Column name: FILTER Type: TEXT Description: Copied from input VCF. This includes filters implemented directly by the variant caller and other external software used in the DNA-Seq pipeline
Column name: VARIANT_CLASS Type: TEXT Description: Sequence Ontology variant class
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 2. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: HGVSp Type: TEXT Description: Protein sequence of the variant in HGVS recommended format. p.= signifies no change in the protein
Column name: CCDS Type: TEXT Description: CCDS identifier for this transcript, where applicable
Column name: INTRON Type: TEXT Description: Intron number (out of total number)
Column name: End_Position Type: NUMBER Description: End position, in 1-based integer coordinates
Column name: Protein_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of affected amino acid in protein. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in coding sequence
Column name: EXON Type: TEXT Description: Exon number (out of total number)
Column name: Transcript_ID Type: TEXT Description: Ensembl ID of the transcript affected by the variant
Column name: Start_Position Type: NUMBER Description: Lowest numeric position of the reported variant on the genomic reference sequence. Mutation start coordinate
Column name: n_alt_count Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth supporting the variant allele in normal BAM (cleared in somatic MAF)
Column name: Feature Type: TEXT Description: Stable Ensembl ID of feature (transcript, regulatory, motif)
Column name: UNIPARC Type: TEXT Description: UniParc identifier of protein product
Column name: DBVS Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list eg byCluster|by1000G
Column name: TREMBL Type: TEXT Description: UniProtKB/TrEMBL identifier of protein product
Column name: GMAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes
Column name: Amino_acids Type: TEXT Description: Amino acid substitution caused by the mutation, only given if the variation affects the protein-coding sequence
Column name: EA_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in NHLBI-ESP European American population
Column name: Consequence Type: TEXT Description: Consequence type of this variant; sequence ontology terms
Column name: case_barcode Type: TEXT Description: Original TCGA case barcode, eg TCGA-12-1089  --  note that each case typically has a primary-tumor sample and a matched-normal (blood or adjacent tissue) sample; please refer to the TCGA Biospecimen table for more details
Column name: CDS_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of base pair in coding sequence. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in coding sequence
Column name: cDNA_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of base pair in the cDNA sequence as a fraction. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in cDNA
Column name: all_effects Type: TEXT Description: A semicolon delimited list of all possible variant effects, sorted by priority ([Symbol,Consequence,HGVSp_Short,Transcript_ID,RefSeq,HGVSc,Impact,Canonical,Sift,PolyPhen,Strand])
Column name: Exon_Number Type: TEXT Description: Exon number (out of total number)
Column name: EUR_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined European population
Column name: Feature_type Type: TEXT Description: Type of feature. Currently one of Transcript, RegulatoryFeature, MotifFeature (or blank)
Column name: HGVSc Type: TEXT Description: Coding sequence of the variant in HGVS recommended format
Column name: t_ref_count Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth supporting the reference allele in tumor BAM
Column name: AFR_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined African population
Column name: Variant_Type Type: TEXT Description: Type of mutation. TNP (tri-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to DNP (di-nucleotide polymorphism) but for three consecutive nucleotides. ONP (oligo-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to TNP but for consecutive runs of four or more (SNP, DNP, TNP, ONP, INS, DEL, or Consolidated)
Column name: EAS_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined East Asian population
Column name: Hugo_Symbol Type: TEXT Description: HUGO symbol for the gene (HUGO symbols are always in all caps). Unknown is used for regions that do not correspond to a gene
Column name: aliquot_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: n_ref_count Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth supporting the reference allele in normal BAM (cleared in somatic MAF)
Column name: IMPACT Type: TEXT Description: Impact modifier for the consequence type
Column name: sample_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: SIFT Type: TEXT Description: SIFT prediction and/or score, with both given as prediction (score)
Column name: Gene Type: TEXT Description: The gene symbol. In this table, gene symbol is simulated data e.g. ENSG00000251562
Column name: PolyPhen Type: TEXT Description: PolyPhen prediction and/or score
Column name: SYMBOL_SOURCE Type: TEXT Description: The source of the gene symbol, usually HGNC, rarely blank, other sources include Uniprot_gn, EntrezGene, etc
Column name: NCALLERS Type: NUMBER Description: Number of callers: a value between 2 and 8 (most common is 5)
Column name: HGVS_OFFSET Type: NUMBER Description: Indicates by how many bases the HGVS notations for this variant have been shifted
Column name: t_alt_count Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth supporting the variant allele in tumor BAM
Column name: aliquot_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: DOMAINS Type: TEXT Description: Source and identifier of any overlapping protein domains
Column name: PHENO Type: TEXT Description: Indicates if existing variant is associated with a phenotype, disease or trait (0, 1, or null)
Column name: COSMIC Type: TEXT Description: Overlapping COSMIC variants
Column name: HGNC_ID Type: NUMBER Description: Gene identifier from the HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee if applicable
Column name: DISTANCE Type: NUMBER Description: Shortest distance from the variant to transcript
Column name: BIOTYPE Type: TEXT Description: Biotype of transcript
Column name: ENSP Type: TEXT Description: Ensembl protein identifier of the affected transcript
Column name: HGVSp_Short Type: TEXT Description: Same as the HGVSp column, but using 1-letter amino-acid codes
Column name: CONTEXT Type: TEXT Description: Reference allele per VCF specs, and its five flanking base pairs
Column name: ASN_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined Asian population
Column name: n_depth Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth across this locus in normal BAM
Column name: SAS_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined South Asian population
Column name: t_depth Type: NUMBER Description: Read depth across this locus in tumor BAM
Column name: Reference_Allele Type: TEXT Description: The plus strand reference allele at this position. Includes the deleted sequence for a deletion or - for an insertion
Column name: SYMBOL Type: TEXT Description: Eg TP53, LRP1B, etc (same as Hugo_Symbol field except blank instead of Unknown
Column name: Chromosome Type: TEXT Description: Chromosome, possible values: 1, X, etc (ie does not include chr prefix)
Column name: NCBI_Build Type: TEXT Description: The reference genome used for the alignment (GRCh37)
Column name: sample_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: CALLERS Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list of mutation caller(s) that agreed on this particular call, always in alphabetical order: muse, mutect, somaticsniper, varscan
Sample rows:
[{'project_short_name': 'TCGA-STAD', 'case_barcode': 'TCGA-R5-A7ZI', 'sample_barcode_tumor': 'TCGA-R5-A7ZI-01A', 'sample_barcode_normal': 'TCGA-R5-A7ZI-10A', 'aliquot_barcode_tumor': 'TCGA-R5-A7ZI-01A-11D-A34U-08', 'aliquot_barcode_normal': 'TCGA-R5-A7ZI-10A-01D-A34X-08', 'Hugo_Symbol': 'CPEB1', 'NCBI_Build': 'GRCh37', 'Chromosome': '15', 'Start_Position': 83240328, 'End_Position': 83240328, 'Variant_Classification': 'Intron', 'Variant_Type': 'DEL', 'Reference_Allele': 'T', 'Tumor_Seq_Allele1': 'T', 'Tumor_Seq_Allele2': '-', 'dbSNP_RS': 'novel', 'HGVSc': 'c.191-46delA', 'HGVSp': None, 'HGVSp_Short': None, 'Transcript_ID': 'ENST00000568128', 'Exon_Number': None, 't_depth': 34, 't_ref_count': 28, 't_alt_count': 6, 'n_depth': 35, 'n_ref_count': 35, 'n_alt_count': 0, 'all_effects': 'CPEB1,5_prime_UTR_variant,,ENST00000423133,;CPEB1,intron_variant,,ENST00000564522,;CPEB1,intron_variant,,ENST00000568128,;CPEB1,intron_variant,,ENST00000567678,;CPEB1,intron_variant,,ENST00000568757,;CPEB1,intr


